import test.{expectEqual, expectTrue}

-- A fixture for the medaka_test MCP tool (#2339): `test` decls ONLY, and both
-- of them fail.  `doctest_sample.mdk` carries no `test` decl at all, so its
-- `testDeclsSkipped:true` is trivially true — nothing was there to skip, and
-- the golden cannot show what the flag costs.  Here the skipped decls are the
-- file's entire content, so the golden records what an agent is actually told
-- about a file whose every assertion failed.
--
-- The golden PINS that report; it does not endorse it.  `summary.ok` and
-- `isError` there describe a file that passed, which is the whole of #2339's
-- complaint — a fix moves this golden rather than leaving it alone.
--
-- Deterministic and prelude-only apart from `test` itself: no timings, no
-- paths, no RNG.

double : Int -> Int
double n = n * 2

test "double 3 is deliberately expected to be 7" = expectEqual (double 3) 7

test "a deliberately false claim" = expectTrue (1 == 2)
